{% layout none %}
{%- comment -%}
  llms.txt — a plain-text brief for AI assistants and answer engines.

  Follows the llmstxt.org shape: an H1 naming the entity, a blockquote summary, then
  link sections. Assistants that fetch it get the store's structure and core facts in
  one request instead of inferring them from rendered HTML.

  `{% layout none %}` strips the theme chrome so the response body is the file itself.

  Everything below is generated from live store data — store details, published
  collections, pages, blogs and policies. Nothing is hard-coded and nothing is invented,
  so the file cannot drift out of date as the catalogue changes. The only editorial text
  comes from the page's own body content in the admin, which is appended at the end as
  an "About" section if the merchant has written anything there.

  SETUP (one-off, in the Shopify admin):
    1. Online Store → Pages → Add page. Title "llms.txt", so the handle becomes
       `llms-txt`. Leave the body empty, or write a short paragraph about the business.
    2. Under Theme template, choose "llms-txt". Save.
    3. Navigation → URL Redirects → Create: redirect `/llms.txt` to `/pages/llms-txt`.
       Shopify serves theme files only from its own fixed paths, so this redirect is what
       makes the conventional root URL resolve.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign origin = request.origin
  assign summary = shop.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | strip
  if summary == blank
    assign summary = shop.name
  endif
-%}
